          "raw_output": "```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"say\",\n  \"text\": \"Excellent \u2014 thank you all for flagging these issues. This is exactly why we do this pre-launch review. Let me summarize what I'm hearing and identify the key conflicts we need to resolve before I can sign off.\\n\\nFirst, Jonas, you're telling us the full $18M issuance could qualify for a green label, but our green-bond framework would require a green label, annual allocation reporting, and an external review if we go that route.\\n\\nHowever, Victor, you've identified a critical conflict: $10M of the $18M must go to refinancing 2027 debt, leaving only $8M for environmental projects. That means the full $18M is NOT available for green projects, which directly affects whether we can apply a green label to the entire issuance.\\n\\nSecond, Maya, the anchor investor wants a 4-year maturity and a coupon no higher than 5.25%, which conflicts with our preliminary 3-year, 5.50% structure. We need to decide whether to adjust terms to accommodate this anchor or proceed with the current structure.\\n\\nThird, Leah, legal requires a make-whole redemption clause and a 12-month no-redemption period, both of which are absent from the preliminary term sheet.\\n\\nSo we have several decisions to make. Let me ask: Jonas, given that only $8M of proceeds would go to environmental projects, can we still label the full $18M bond as green, or would we need to restructure? And Maya, how critical is this anchor investor to the success of the book?\"\n}\n```"
